/*
 * The table of contents for the API Reference.
 *
 * Doxygen orders groups by where each one is first defined, and this file
 * comes first in the INPUT of the Doxyfile. So the order here is the order
 * of the sidebar and of the topics page. Headers add to these groups with
 * `@addtogroup`, which is where the text of each group lives.
 *
 * The id of a group is its URL, so don't change one.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup api_terminal Terminal
 * @brief The terminal itself.
 *
 * Start with @ref terminal. It holds the screen, scrollback, cursor and
 * modes, and it's where you write VT data. @ref effects are the callbacks
 * that answer what a program asks of the terminal.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup terminal Terminal
 * @ingroup api_terminal
 * @brief Create a terminal, write VT data to it, and read its state.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup effects Effects
 * @ingroup api_terminal
 * @brief Respond to what programs ask of the terminal, such as the bell,
 * title changes, and queries.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup modes Modes
 * @ingroup api_terminal
 * @brief Pack DEC and ANSI mode numbers and encode DECRPM reports.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup snapshot Snapshots
 * @ingroup api_terminal
 * @brief Save a terminal's full state and restore it later.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup api_screen Screen Contents
 * @brief Read what is on the screen.
 *
 * A terminal's contents are a grid of cells. Find a cell with a @ref point
 * "point" or a @ref grid_ref "grid reference", then read its text and
 * @ref style "style". @ref selection, @ref search and @ref formatter work
 * across many cells at once.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup screen Cells and Rows
 * @ingroup api_screen
 * @brief Read the contents of grid cells and rows.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup point Points
 * @ingroup api_screen
 * @brief Name a grid position in the active area, viewport, screen, or
 * history.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup grid_ref Grid References
 * @ingroup api_screen
 * @brief Point at a cell, read it, and keep track of it as the terminal
 * scrolls.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup style Style
 * @ingroup api_screen
 * @brief Read a cell's colors and text attributes.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup selection Selection
 * @ingroup api_screen
 * @brief Select words, lines, and ranges, and turn pointer gestures into
 * selections.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup search Search
 * @ingroup api_screen
 * @brief Find a string in a terminal, including its scrollback.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup formatter Formatter
 * @ingroup api_screen
 * @brief Turn terminal content into plain text, VT sequences, or HTML.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup api_rendering Rendering
 * @brief Draw a terminal.
 *
 * @ref render tells you what changed since the last frame and gives you the
 * rows and cells to draw. @ref kitty_graphics tells you which images to draw
 * and where.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup render Render State
 * @ingroup api_rendering
 * @brief Find out what changed since the last frame and read the rows and
 * cells to draw.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup kitty_graphics Kitty Graphics
 * @ingroup api_rendering
 * @brief Read the images that programs send with the Kitty graphics
 * protocol.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup api_input Input
 * @brief Turn user input into bytes for the pty.
 *
 * Keys, mouse events, focus changes and pastes all reach a program as bytes
 * on the pty. These topics produce those bytes.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup key Keys
 * @ingroup api_input
 * @brief Encode key events with the legacy encoding or the Kitty keyboard
 * protocol.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup mouse Mouse
 * @ingroup api_input
 * @brief Encode mouse events with the X10, UTF-8, SGR, URxvt, or SGR-Pixels
 * protocols.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup focus Focus
 * @ingroup api_input
 * @brief Encode focus gained and lost events, for mode 1004.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup paste Paste
 * @ingroup api_input
 * @brief Paste into a terminal, and check paste data for unsafe content.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup api_building_blocks Building Blocks
 * @brief Parsers and encoders that work without a terminal.
 *
 * Each of these works on its own, with no GhosttyTerminal. Use them when you
 * need one piece of terminal behavior and not a whole terminal.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup osc OSC Parser
 * @ingroup api_building_blocks
 * @brief Parse OSC sequences into commands.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup sgr SGR Parser
 * @ingroup api_building_blocks
 * @brief Parse SGR sequences into text attributes.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup size_report Size Reports
 * @ingroup api_building_blocks
 * @brief Encode size reports, for mode 2048 and XTWINOPS queries.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup color_scheme Color Scheme Reports
 * @ingroup api_building_blocks
 * @brief Encode the reply to a color scheme query (CSI ? 996 n).
 */

/**
 * @defgroup color Colors
 * @ingroup api_building_blocks
 * @brief Parse colors, generate palettes, and look up X11 color names.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup unicode Unicode
 * @ingroup api_building_blocks
 * @brief Measure codepoints and graphemes the way the terminal does.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup api_library Library
 * @brief Types and settings shared by every API.
 *
 * These apply across the library: the result codes and buffers that every
 * function uses, what this build of the library contains, and how it reaches
 * memory and the system.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup core_types Core Types
 * @ingroup api_library
 * @brief The result codes, strings, and buffers that every API uses.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup version Version
 * @ingroup api_library
 * @brief Check which version of libghostty-vt you are using.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup build_info Build Info
 * @ingroup api_library
 * @brief Find out how this copy of the library was built and which features
 * it has.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup allocator Allocators
 * @ingroup api_library
 * @brief Run the library on your own memory allocator.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup io Readers and Writers
 * @ingroup api_library
 * @brief Stream bytes in and out through your own callbacks.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup sys System Interface
 * @ingroup api_library
 * @brief Plug in your own system functions, such as a PNG decoder.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup wasm WebAssembly
 * @ingroup api_library
 * @brief Allocate memory and pass pointers from a WebAssembly host.
 */
